1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:03,167
When Life Doesn't Go as Planned

2
00:00:03,233 --> 00:00:04,467
Deeply Rooted

3
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:06,533
Episode One

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,700
Have you ever looked at your life…

5
00:00:08,767 --> 00:00:11,200
…and wondered how you ended up here?

6
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:14,700
Not because everything is terrible.

7
00:00:14,767 --> 00:00:15,900
But because…

8
00:00:15,967 --> 00:00:18,267
this isn't where you thought you would be.

9
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:19,733
You had plans.

10
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,267
You had dreams.

11
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:23,400
You imagined a different version of yourself

12
00:00:23,467 --> 00:00:24,400
by now.

13
00:00:24,467 --> 00:00:26,267
Maybe you thought you'd be happier,

14
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:28,900
more successful, more loved.

15
00:00:28,967 --> 00:00:30,233
Maybe you thought certain people

16
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,033
would still be beside you.

17
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,200
Maybe you believed that by this age,

18
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,533
by this moment,

19
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:38,033
everything would finally make sense.

20
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:40,533
But life… had other plans.

21
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:42,400
And sometimes the hardest part

22
00:00:42,467 --> 00:00:43,867
isn't what happened.

23
00:00:43,933 --> 00:00:45,033
It's learning to accept

24
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:46,667
that the life you imagined

25
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:49,567
may never look exactly the way you expected.

26
00:00:49,633 --> 00:00:51,933
But what if you're not falling behind?

27
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,700
What if you're simply living a chapter

28
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:55,467
you never knew you needed?

29
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:57,300
We spend so much of our lives

30
00:00:57,367 --> 00:00:58,367
measuring ourselves

31
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:00,267
against invisible timelines.

32
00:01:00,467 --> 00:01:02,933
"By this age, I should have achieved this."

33
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,400
"By now, I should have found my purpose."

34
00:01:05,467 --> 00:01:06,933
"I should be further ahead."

35
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,433
"I should be happier."

36
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,233
And without even realizing it,

37
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:11,933
we turn our lives into a race

38
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,467
against a version of ourselves

39
00:01:13,533 --> 00:01:15,333
that doesn't even exist.

40
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:17,433
We forget that people grow differently,

41
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:18,700
heal differently,

42
00:01:18,767 --> 00:01:20,733
discover themselves differently.

43
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:22,900
Some people find their direction early.

44
00:01:22,967 --> 00:01:25,000
Others spend years searching.

45
00:01:25,067 --> 00:01:27,600
Some find love when they least expect it.

46
00:01:27,667 --> 00:01:28,833
Others need time to learn

47
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:30,667
how to love themselves first.

48
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:32,267
And some of the strongest people

49
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:33,333
you'll ever meet

50
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,233
are still figuring things out.

51
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,100
There is no universal timeline

52
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:39,033
for becoming who you are meant to be.

53
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:40,267
Your journey doesn't become

54
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:41,633
less meaningful just because

55
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,767
it looks different from someone else's.

56
00:01:43,833 --> 00:01:44,867
So please,

57
00:01:44,933 --> 00:01:47,167
stop treating your life like a deadline.

58
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:49,000
You are a human being,

59
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,933
not a project that needs to be completed

60
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,567
by a certain age.

61
00:01:53,867 --> 00:01:54,767
And then,

62
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:57,367
there are the things we never wanted to lose.

63
00:01:57,433 --> 00:01:58,533
A relationship.

64
00:01:58,600 --> 00:01:59,700
An opportunity.

65
00:01:59,767 --> 00:02:02,067
A dream we worked so hard for.

66
00:02:02,133 --> 00:02:03,367
A version of life we thought

67
00:02:03,433 --> 00:02:05,233
was finally within reach.

68
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:08,200
Losing something you truly wanted hurts.

69
00:02:08,267 --> 00:02:10,433
And you don't have to pretend otherwise.

70
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,433
You don't have to call

71
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:12,967
every disappointment a blessing

72
00:02:13,033 --> 00:02:15,100
while you're still trying to understand it.

73
00:02:15,167 --> 00:02:16,700
Sometimes you just need

74
00:02:16,767 --> 00:02:18,033
to sit with the feeling.

75
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:19,800
To acknowledge that it mattered.

76
00:02:19,867 --> 00:02:20,900
That you cared.

77
00:02:20,967 --> 00:02:22,100
That you hoped.

78
00:02:22,167 --> 00:02:23,800
And that it hurts.

79
00:02:25,067 --> 00:02:26,933
But don't let one painful chapter

80
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,633
convince you that the entire story is over.

81
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,567
A closed door is not proof

82
00:02:31,633 --> 00:02:34,033
that every door will remain closed.

83
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:35,300
A difficult season

84
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:37,467
is not a permanent identity.

85
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:39,067
And a moment of uncertainty

86
00:02:39,133 --> 00:02:41,567
doesn't mean you've lost your way forever.

87
00:02:41,733 --> 00:02:42,867
Sometimes,

88
00:02:42,933 --> 00:02:45,800
the most important growth happens quietly.

89
00:02:45,867 --> 00:02:47,467
When nobody is watching.

90
00:02:47,533 --> 00:02:49,900
When there are no achievements to celebrate.

91
00:02:49,967 --> 00:02:52,633
When all you're doing is choosing to get up

92
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:53,933
and try again.

93
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,367
That matters too.

94
00:02:55,433 --> 00:02:57,467
Maybe you need to hear this today:

95
00:02:57,533 --> 00:02:59,833
You are allowed to begin again.

96
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,000
You are allowed to change your mind.

97
00:03:02,067 --> 00:03:03,533
You are allowed to outgrow

98
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,133
the dreams you once had.

99
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,767
You are allowed to walk away

100
00:03:06,833 --> 00:03:08,767
from what no longer feels right.

101
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:10,200
And you are allowed to build

102
00:03:10,267 --> 00:03:12,033
a completely different life,

103
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:14,500
even if it takes longer than you imagined.

104
00:03:14,567 --> 00:03:16,567
Don't underestimate the quiet courage

105
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:18,033
it takes to keep going.

106
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:20,167
Not every victory is visible.

107
00:03:20,233 --> 00:03:22,100
Sometimes victory is getting through

108
00:03:22,167 --> 00:03:24,867
a difficult day without giving up on yourself.

109
00:03:24,933 --> 00:03:26,800
Sometimes it's choosing peace

110
00:03:26,867 --> 00:03:28,133
over proving a point.

111
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:30,033
Sometimes it's forgiving yourself

112
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,800
for the years you spent not knowing

113
00:03:31,867 --> 00:03:33,033
what you know today.

114
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:34,267
And sometimes,

115
00:03:34,333 --> 00:03:36,433
it's simply trusting that your story

116
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:39,300
still has beautiful pages left to be written.

117
00:03:39,367 --> 00:03:40,567
And perhaps

118
00:03:40,633 --> 00:03:42,833
there is another way to look at all of this.

119
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:45,033
A way that invites us to loosen our grip

120
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:47,000
on the things we cannot control.

121
00:03:47,067 --> 00:03:48,967
In the Qur'an, Allah reminds us

122
00:03:49,033 --> 00:03:51,700
in Surah Al-Baqarah, verse 216:

123
00:03:51,767 --> 00:03:53,267
"But perhaps you hate a thing

124
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:54,667
and it is good for you;

125
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:56,133
and perhaps you love a thing

126
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,633
and it is bad for you.

127
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:00,500
And Allah knows, while you know not."

128
00:04:02,433 --> 00:04:03,900
Think about that for a moment.

129
00:04:03,967 --> 00:04:06,800
How often have we wanted something so deeply,

130
00:04:06,867 --> 00:04:09,200
believing it was exactly what we needed?

131
00:04:09,267 --> 00:04:10,833
And how often have we looked back

132
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:12,333
at something we once considered

133
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,333
a disappointment,

134
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,267
only to realize that life took us

135
00:04:15,333 --> 00:04:17,233
somewhere we couldn't have imagined.

136
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:19,467
This doesn't mean every painful experience

137
00:04:19,533 --> 00:04:21,167
will immediately make sense.

138
00:04:21,233 --> 00:04:22,800
And it doesn't mean you're not allowed

139
00:04:22,867 --> 00:04:24,267
to grieve what you lost.

140
00:04:24,333 --> 00:04:25,633
It simply reminds us

141
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,800
that our perspective is limited.

142
00:04:27,867 --> 00:04:29,167
We see a moment.

143
00:04:29,233 --> 00:04:31,033
God knows the whole picture.

144
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:34,100
And sometimes faith means taking the next step

145
00:04:34,167 --> 00:04:36,900
even when you cannot see the entire road.

146
00:04:36,967 --> 00:04:39,933
So, if life doesn't look the way you planned,

147
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
take a breath.

148
00:04:41,067 --> 00:04:43,067
You haven't missed your only chance.

149
00:04:43,133 --> 00:04:44,600
You haven't become less worthy

150
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:46,133
because things took longer.

151
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,467
And you don't need to have

152
00:04:47,533 --> 00:04:48,800
every answer tonight.

153
00:04:48,867 --> 00:04:49,867
Keep growing.

154
00:04:49,933 --> 00:04:50,933
Keep learning.

155
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Keep becoming.

156
00:04:52,067 --> 00:04:53,667
And don't forget to appreciate

157
00:04:53,733 --> 00:04:56,033
the person you're becoming along the way.

158
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,100
Because life isn't only about reaching

159
00:04:58,167 --> 00:05:00,400
the destination you once imagined.

160
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:03,233
It's also about discovering who you become

161
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,600
along the journey.

162
00:05:04,667 --> 00:05:06,500
And wherever you are right now,

163
00:05:06,567 --> 00:05:09,133
I hope you find the courage to keep going.

164
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,067
Not because everything is certain,

165
00:05:11,133 --> 00:05:14,300
but because your story is still unfolding.

166
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:17,700
This is Deeply Rooted.

167
00:05:17,767 --> 00:05:20,233
A place to pause, to reflect,

168
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,700
and to remember what truly matters.

169
00:05:22,767 --> 00:05:23,900
Until next time,

170
00:05:23,967 --> 00:05:26,200
stay grounded, stay hopeful,

171
00:05:26,267 --> 00:05:28,600
and stay deeply rooted.
